  "ingredients": [
    "4 skinless, boneless chicken breast halves",
    "1 cup barbecue sauce",
    "22 ounces sauerkraut"
  ],
  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Gather all ingredients. Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C).",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/s97Gp1A0OAkW96u8ovAR1lzluhM=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/8781-german-chicken-VAT-step-01-d3de43abeb26423e987ccca7b3d63af7.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/8781/step_01.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Place sauerkraut in a single layer in a 9x13-inch baking dish. Place chicken breasts on top of sauerkraut. Pour barbecue sauce over chicken.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/mOCAueETkscq381CQzSMCkTXhg8=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/8781-german-chicken-VAT-step-02-54c5a4f5bf3747219bee81c7561a2a2e.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/8781/step_02.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Cover and bake in the preheated oven until chicken is no longer pink and the juices run clear, about 30 to 40 minutes. An instant-read thermometer inserted into the center should read 165 degrees F (74 degrees C).",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
